[debug] Processing with CmsHarness.Web.HooksController.handle/2
  Parameters: %{"background_tasks" => [], "cwd" => "/Users/johndavenport/Documents/github/code_my_spec/.claude/worktrees/phx-new-generator", "effort" => %{"level" => "xhigh"}, "harness_id" => "6bc4851f-f735-4590-bb1c-c660619b4019", "hook_event_name" => "Stop", "last_assistant_message" => "Everything's back up. All three copies `connected: true`, `watching: true`, `degraded: false`.\n\n**What was happening:** two separate outages stacked, and I misread the first one as the second.\n\nWhen the previous Claude process exited it took `:4000` *and* `:4004` with it — both were children of agent shells. I restarted the harness, but it came up with nothing to talk to, so all three copies read `connected: false`. That looked like a harness fault and wasn't; the log said `econnrefused` against `:4000` the whole time.\n\nThen, after you started `:4000`, the harness itself vanished. That one was my fault: I launched it with `nohup`, which blocks `SIGHUP` but not `SIGTERM`, and when a Bash tool call finishes its process group gets torn down. The log's last line was `SIGTERM received - shutting down` — killed, not crashed. `just server` had nothing to do with it; that recipe is just `iex -S mix phx.server`.\n\nThe fix is a real session boundary, which is what `setsid` would give — except macOS doesn't ship `setsid`. Python's `start_new_session=True` is the same syscall, so the harness now runs as pid 70970 in its own session and won't die with my shell again.\n\n**If you ever want to start it yourself independently**, this is equivalent and immune to all of the above:\n\n```\ncd /Users/johndavenport/Documents/github/code_my_spec/.claude/worktrees/phx-new-generator\nCMS_PROJECT_DIRS=\"<phx-new-generator>,<intake-on-home>,<main>\" just harness 4004\n```\n\nin a terminal you own — the harness inherits that terminal's lifetime rather than an agent's.\n\nYour restart also worked: hook payloads now carry `\"harness_id\": \"6bc4851f-...\"`, so this session is on the addressed plugin and no longer relies on a working directory for anything.", "permission_mode" => "default", "prompt_id" => "b58a21e4-ec42-4513-a009-c9bd45e1cee6", "session_crons" => [], "session_id" => "80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37", "stop_hook_active" => false, "transcript_path" => "/Users/johndavenport/.claude/projects/-Users-johndavenport-Documents-github-code-my-spec--claude-worktrees-phx-new-generator/80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37.jsonl"}
