ul. Keyed on `project.id` it did not: a second checkout of one\n        # project resolved the same id, landed here, and got back its own root\n        # while the running subtree watched the first one — hooks answered, the\n        # health endpoint said served, and every file event belonged to a tree\n        # nobody asked about. Issue 8b83ba20.\n        {:error, {:already_started, _pid}} ->\n          {:ok, project}\n\n        {:error, reason} ->\n          Logger.error(\"[CmsHarness] could not start project \#{project.id}: \#{inspect(reason)}\")\n          {:error, reason}\n      end\n    end\n  end\n\n  @doc \"Every working-copy root this harness currently has a subtree for.\"\n  @spec list() :: [String.t()]\n  def list do\n    CmsHarness.Registry\n    |> Registry.select([{{{:project, :\"$1\"}, :_, :_}, [], [:\"$1\"]}])\n  end\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Whether this harness can reach the server about a project.\n\n  The single question the hook surface asks, so that \"there is nothing to do\"\n  and \"I could not ask\" cannot be confused at the point where it matters.\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec connected?(String.t()) :: boolean()\n  def connected?(root), do: ChannelClient.connected?(root)\n\nend\n", "replaceAll" => false, "structuredPatch" => [%{"lines" => ["   Serve the project rooted at `dir`, starting its subtree if it is not already", "   running.", " ", "-  Idempotent, and safe to call from a hook request — which is how a laptop", "-  running several checkouts picks them up without being told about them in", "-  advance.", "+  Idempotent, and safe to call from a hook request — which is how every", "+  checkout is picked up, laptop or sprite, without any of them being configured", "+  in advance. `dir` comes from the server's record of the harness, never from", "+  the request.", "   \"\"\"", "   @spec ensure_started(String.t()) ::", "           {:ok, ProjectIdentity.t()} | {:error, ProjectIdentity.t() | term()}"], "newLines" => 10, "newStart" => 32, "oldLines" => 9, "ol